<title>ITALY: Finmeccanica,GEC discuss j-venture.</title>
<headline>Finmeccanica,GEC discuss j-venture.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Industry Minister Pierluigi Bersani said on Wednesday that talks were in progress on a joint-venture between state-owned engineering group Finmeccanica and Britain's General Electric Co Plc.</p>
<p>&quot;Work is in course on the prospect of a joint venture,&quot; Bersani told reporters in response to a question on a link-up between Finmeccanica and GEC-Marconi, a unit of GEC.</p>
<p>The two companies said in London on Monday that talks were in progress, and proceeding well, on a defence cooperation, but said the purchase of the defence operations of one company by the other was not on the cards.</p>
<p>Bersani also confirmed that Finmeccanica's restructuring plan was &quot;pretty imminent&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
